\'a0 Thank you for sharing the photos of your new installation \'97 great to see, and good to know your team keeps raising the bar.\
\'a0\
\'a0 To answer your question directly: our project hasn't stalled on budget or design \'97 it's waiting on four specific technical points from your civil engineer that you flagged as pending when you replied to our first batch of questions (quotation BS04H092126). Since you mentioned he's back from his site visits, could you follow up with him on these four items?\
\'a0\
\'a0 1. Expansion ceiling for our specific configuration: now that we understand the real per-set footprint is ~1.2 m (not the ~3.4 m we had mis-calculated before), how many additional sets can the same feeding/egg-collection line we already ordered actually support before a second complete shared system is needed?\
\'a0 2. Foundation extensibility: can the foundation be extended lengthwise in stages without rebuilding it? After how many sets (or what length) would a structural reinforcement or expansion joint be required?\
\'a0 3. Manure belt throughput: what is the real throughput (kg/h) of the belt already quoted? We need it to handle approximately 1,000 kg/day once we reach our medium-term target of ~5,120 birds \'97 can the current belt support that, or would a different model be needed?\
\'a0 4. Transverse footprint: what is the cage depth + central aisle of the double-sided, 4-level arrangement? We need to confirm it fits within our 4 m width.\
\'a0\
\'a0 Once we have these four, we'll be in a good position to move forward on the civil works design \'97 and we'll send our remaining questions on ventilation, water/manure treatment, and electrical specs in the same consolidated batches we mentioned before, so your team isn't juggling too many threads at once.\
\'a0\
\'a0 Thanks again for staying on top of this \'97 looking forward to hearing back.\
\'a0\
